! Nowledge Mem synchronization

Every saved user tiddler has a Nowledge Mem toolbar button. The button creates a linked Memory, pushes a local-only change, pulls a remote-only change, does nothing when both snapshots are current, and reports a conflict when both sides changed.

Only tiddlers listed in [[$:/StoryList]] are checked. The plugin does not poll or scan closed tiddlers.

!! Required plugin

Production installs require [[$:/plugins/linonetwo/markdown-transformer]] for WikiText pulls. `tw-nowledge` calls its public `md2tid` library module; `nr dev` and the standalone demo load the verified dependency automatically, while `Nowledge.tid` does not bundle it.

!! Configuration

|Setting | Tiddler | Default |
|Nowledge Mem API URL | [[$:/config/tw-nowledge/api-url]] | `http://127.0.0.1:14242` |
|Space ID | [[$:/config/tw-nowledge/space-id]] | `default` |
|Portable Wiki identity | [[$:/config/tw-nowledge/wiki-id]] | `auto` (derived from the wiki and location) |
|Temporary API key | [[$:/temp/tw-nowledge/api-key]] | empty |

These defaults are shadow tiddlers. Editing one creates a user override; deleting the override restores the plugin default. The API key tiddler is temporary and must not be persisted. When using `tiddlynmem` and this plugin together, set the same Wiki identity here and pass it to the importer with `--wiki-id`.
